00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:24.880
Kent Dybvig: So I think one concrete example is if we wanted to have… A…

83
00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:30.910
Kent Dybvig: The ability to have a single compiler that either targets

84
00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:37.209
Kent Dybvig: you know, a single compact C, or a single compact updater, whichever.

85
00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:41.809
Kent Dybvig: They're totally different approaches to the same problem.

86
00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:52.899
