00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:42.759
Kevin Millikin (Shielded Technologies): compilation pipelines alive, one with the inefficient way of doing that, in case somebody needs to downgrade to 3.0, and one with the more, better, efficient way. I would just like a release that just is like, here's the improvements.

143
00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:44.430
Kent Dybvig: Yeah, because… I agree.

144
00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:54.980
Kevin Millikin (Shielded Technologies): because you don't… because you don't care about the… because you don't care about the ZKIR version. It's just… It's just another… it's a back-end artifact that the user shouldn't know about, for the most part. Go ahead, Joe.

